# Several compute machines: Preferences > Compute with two machines (one switched off), Use one against Share, and a solve shared by
# three machines (scripted: a real one takes minutes and the driver waits for running tasks; `share-mid` is the drag part of a solve with two
# points in flight, `angle-share-mid` the angles part of it). Seed the settings and run:
#   cat > /tmp/share-settings.json <<'JSON'
#   {"compute":{"machines":[{"target":"sandvoxel@192.168.1.88","enabled":true},
#                           {"target":"lab@192.168.1.99","enabled":false,"label":"Lab"}],
#               "use_this_computer":true,"mode":"share"}}
#   JSON
#   BOWSHOCK_SETTINGS_FILE=/tmp/share-settings.json BOWSHOCK_CFD_DEMO=share-mid,angle-share-mid \
#     cargo run --release -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/share-compute.drive out/share-compute
# `Test connection` talks to the real host over SSH (key auth; the first run sets the worker up there).
viewport 1300x800
click "Analyze"

# The shared drag solve: the left panel lists the machines, the chart rings two points, the strips show one row per busy machine.
click "CFD table"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot share-1-solve-shared.png

# Preferences > Compute: Share across all switched-on machines (the machine that is off is not used or contacted).
click "Change…"
screenshot share-2-prefs-share.png

# Use one: pick among the machines that are on.
click "Use one"
screenshot share-3-prefs-pick.png

# Back to sharing, and test the machine that is on against the real host.
click "Share across all switched-on machines"
click "Test connection"
screenshot share-4-prefs-tested.png
click "Done"

# The same solve in its angles, shared by the same machines.
click "Cancel"
click "Discard"
click "Re-solve"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot share-5-solve-3d-shared.png
